senses.gloss:
(I)--a name given to the thirteen sons of the Kings of किलिकिला;
1: भा. XII. 1. ३४.
took part in the राजसूय of युधिष्- ठिर;
2: Ib. X. ७५. 6.
three of the thirteen sons were of the Nandana family; Ekalas or lords of small regions.
3: Vi. IV. २४. ५७. ५८.

(I)--a son of Pratipa and father of Soma- datta;
1: भा. IX. २२. १२ and १८; ४९. 2; वा. ९९. २३४; Vi. IV. २०. 9; V. ३५. १२, २७, ३०.
father of seven sons, kings of बाह्लि Kingdom;
2: M. ५०. ३९.
the [page२-482+ ३७] foremost among the Kurus;
3: भा. X. ५२. ११ [9].
was stationed by जरासन्ध at the southern gate of मथुरा;
4: Ib. X. ५०. ११ [4].
placed on the south dur- ing the siege of Gomanta;
5: Ib. X. ५२. ११ [9].
informed by Uddhava of राम's visit to हस्तिनापुर;
6: Ib. X. ६८. १७.
his sons took active part in युधिष्ठिर's राजसूय and in Duryodana's army;
7: Ib. X. ७५. 6; [९५ (v) १६].
could not vanquish Arjuna, supported by कृष्ण;
8: Ib. I १५. १६.
went with his sons to स्यमन्तपञ्चक for the solar eclipse where he met the वृष्णिस्; left स्यमन्तपञ्चक;
9: Ib. X. ८२. २६; ८४. ६९. [1].
sisters, रोहिणी and पौरवी, married to Vasudeva.
१०: Br. III. ७१. १६३.
